      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/9de053/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2012-10-05T19:34:14.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>For explicit clarification, for the purposes of effects such as Spite's DR, Fixer's Crane Stance, and Nightmist's redirection, does each hero's turn reset these effects, so that Mr. Fixer could redirect the damage from a Rampage, a Grenade Launcher and a sufficiently weak Oblivion during a single round, or is he limited to once per 'overall hero turn?'</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Similarly, and especially for Nightmist, does 'the first time' specifically only refer to the first time Nightmist would take damage, or can she choose to ignore redirecting 1 damage to redirect 4 damage that would hit her instead, such as if she was infected and decided to heedless lash Plague Rat?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:36:21.876Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
