    {
      "id": 39908,
      "name": "Matchstickman",
      "username": "Matchstickman",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/{size}/1880_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-10-05T20:36:53.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ryushikaze\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/9de053/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ryushikaze:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Similarly, and especially for Nightmist, does 'the first time' specifically only refer to the first time Nightmist would take damage, or can she choose to ignore redirecting 1 damage to redirect 4 damage that would hit her instead, such as if she was infected and decided to heedless lash Plague Rat?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The \"first time\" means the first time the condition is met, if you can chose not to use the redirect then you&nbsp; can chose not to use the redirect&nbsp; but you can't choose to redirect something else later as it is no longer \"the first time\" you are damaged this turn.</p>",
